# R/01_simulation_study

Core model-fitting and simulation code underlying the entire paper.

This folder defines the three ETAS estimators compared throughout the
manuscript — classical kernel-based ETAS, its FLP-enhanced version
(ETAS-FLP), and the proposed regression-based background estimator
(ETAS-P) — together with the synthetic-catalogue simulator and the main
simulation plan used to evaluate them.

## Files

- **`etas_parametric_final_plan_no_smooth.R`**
  Defines `etasclass()` (classical ETAS; also fits ETAS-FLP via the
  `flp=TRUE` argument) and `etasclass.par()` (the proposed ETAS-P
  estimator), the ETAS catalogue simulator (`etas.par.sim_v4()`), and
  orchestrates the main simulation plan together with the four original
  secondary sensitivity analyses (catalogue size, background
  misspecification, local background irregularity, extreme triggering).
  Produces Tables S1–S8 of the Supplementary Information and Figures 1–6
  of the main text.

- **`add_etas_flp_to_existing_results_NO_OVERWRITE_v3.R`**
  A companion script that adds the ETAS-FLP fit to catalogues already
  simulated by the main plan above, without overwriting the existing
  ETAS/ETAS-P results for the same replicates. It reads the saved `.rds`
  outputs of the main plan and does not generate any new synthetic data.

## Dependency order

Run `etas_parametric_final_plan_no_smooth.R` first (it defines the
functions used everywhere else in the repository and produces the main
simulation output); `add_etas_flp_to_existing_results_NO_OVERWRITE_v3.R`
is run afterwards, pointed at the same output directory.
